From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 20:20:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Add the pin bank
 supplies

Banks PB, PC and PD have no supply in the DT, so the pin controller
uses dummy regulators for them. PB runs from VCC-IO, which is SWOUT2,
and PC from CLDO5, which now takes its schematic name vcc-pc. PD runs
from VCC33-LCD, which is SWOUT1: in the schematic the VCC-PD ball is
connected to it through R251, not to BLDO2, whose output also carries a
VCC-PD label.

Add the three supplies. The A733 pin controller does not program the
withstand voltage from them, so no register changes.

Not covered: banks PE, PF, PG, PJ and PK, whose supplies are either
not described yet, switched off or dual.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the pin controller holds
vcc33-lcd (SWOUT1) as a consumer.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index d7248efc83eb..e7ef3e436076 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -157,6 +157,9 @@ &osc {
 };
 
 &pio {
+	vcc-pb-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
+	vcc-pc-supply = <&reg_cldo5>;
+	vcc-pd-supply = <&reg_swout1>;
 	vcc-ph-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
 };
 
@@ -181,7 +184,7 @@ reg_dcdc1: dcdc1 {
 
 			/* 1.8 V I/O: eMMC VCCQ, bank PC */
 			reg_cldo5: cldo5 {
-				regulator-name = "vcc-1v8";
+				regulator-name = "vcc-pc";
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
 				regulator-always-on;
